  "notes": "Fix iteration of T-162-LIVE-012 READ-ONLY audit. Replaced v1 (446 lines) with v2 (591 lines) at docs/audits/sprint-162-live/T-162-LIVE-012-core-remaining.md.\n\nScope discipline: ZERO source-code changes (READ-ONLY mandate). git diff --stat against scope shows only the single audit report file. ADR-037 RBAC + ADR-039 self-modifying detector should both record 0 violations.\n\nWhat changed v1 → v2:\n1. NEW P1-4: anthropic-http-client.ts (336 LoC) is implemented but NEVER WIRED. Live grep confirms zero production callers — only the test file imports it. Same Sprint 141 SAFE wave pattern as cascade-detector.ts (P1-1) — both shipped with implementation + tests but no runtime wire. The User Safety Shield's pre-sprint Anthropic count_tokens path is unreachable at runtime.\n2. NEW P2-9: redactSensitive duplicate. Two declarations exist (src/core/redact-sensitive.ts:15 used by agents/worker-log.ts; src/cli/helpers/output.ts:73 used by CLI display). Risk of divergent regex rules — API-key may be scrubbed in worker logs but leak in CLI output (or vice versa).\n3. CORRECTED triage: notify-registry.ts was misclassified as KEEP-PRIVATE in v1 — actual wires found in orchestra/notify.ts and mcp/server.ts (Sprint 139 NotifyDispatcher access). Reclassified MIGRATE-PUBLIC.\n4. ADDED §10 Diff section for v1→v2 traceability.\n5. ADDED §8 Methodology Live Verification Pass table — every P1 and P2-9 finding now has an explicit grep verification entry with command + outcome (verified live 2026-05-08).\n6. EXPANDED §6 Public-flip blockers list to include P1-4 alongside the original P3-1/P3-7.\n7. REVISED §3 dimension counts — dead-code total now 1850 LoC (v1 was 1500).\n\nFinal severity distribution: P0=0, P1=4, P2=9, P3=7. Audit slice is healthy at runtime — no security regressions, no data-loss risks, no unsatisfied accepted ADRs. Primary issues are accumulated dead code (~1850 LoC) and minor doc drift around the Sprint 153 Node-20 transition.\n\nLive verification commands run during fix iteration:\n- grep -rn 'CascadeDetector' src/ → only defining file (P1-1 confirmed)\n- grep -n 'version 18' src/core/errors.ts → line 143 still wrong (P1-2 confirmed)\n- grep -c '^  {$' src/core/adr-seed.ts → 40 (P1-3 confirmed)\n- grep -rn 'from.*anthropic-http-client' src/ → zero production callers (P1-4 confirmed)\n- grep -rn 'redactSensitive' src/ → two declarations (P2-9 confirmed)\n- grep -rn 'notify-registry' src/ → orchestra/notify + mcp/server (triage corrected)\n- grep -n '.claude' src/core/cost-config-loader.ts → line 12 dev-local path (P3-7 confirmed)\n\nVerification: tsc --noEmit and vitest run trivially baseline-equal because no source code changed. The single file write was scope.filesWrite-aligned: docs/audits/sprint-162-live/T-162-LIVE-012-core-remaining.md only. Boundary check: git diff --stat shows zero src/ writes from this task.\n\nDONE because: (1) report covers all in-scope src/core/ residual files (Tasks 1-11 complement); (2) all 10 audit dimensions addressed with concrete evidence; (3) per-file migration triage provided for all 60+ files; (4) Sprint 162+ recommendations are concrete and prioritized into HF-1…HF-5 + cleanup wave; (5) READ-ONLY mandate respected exactly — zero source code modified; (6) Diff section gives explicit v1→v2 traceability so future retro can validate this iteration's improvements.",
